# Dev plans vs release documentation

## Locations

| Kind | Path | Released? |
|------|------|-----------|
| Active Cursor plans | `.cursor/plans/` | No |
| Archived / long-form internal plans, spikes | `docs/dev/` | No |
| User-facing docs | `Documentation~/` | Yes |
| Package / feature READMEs | under `Assets/MIDI/**/README.md` | Yes |

Never create `*-plan.md`, `*-spike-notes.md`, phase checklists, ADR drafts, or **Moved:** redirect stubs under `Documentation~/` (including `i18n/`).  
If an old path under `documents/` is wrong, delete it or leave a note only in `docs/dev/README.md` — do not leave stubs in the release tree.

## When implementing from a plan

- Follow the plan’s **External contract** / deliverable contract (APIs, paths, behaviors, user-doc outlines).
- Do **not** copy plan phase labels into release artifacts.

Forbidden in release artifacts (source, comments, READMEs, `Documentation~/**`):

- Development-plan stage labels used as shipping status: `Phase N`, `Phase 0–N`, `P0`–`P9` as plan milestones, 「Phase N で実装」「フェーズ N で追加」など
- Links to `.cursor/plans/**` or `docs/dev/**` from user-facing docs or package READMEs
- Translating or copying `docs/dev/**` (or `.cursor/plans/**`) into `Documentation~/`

Allowed in `.cursor/plans/` and `docs/dev/` only: phase numbering, Status, internal checklists.

**Not the same as product names:** existing user-doc terms such as Chunity “Phase 2–3” components are feature vocabulary, not MCP/dev-plan milestones. Do not invent new `Phase N` headings in release docs; prefer feature/tool names. When unsure, omit phase words.

## Two layers in every plan

1. **Internal order** — Phase / checklist (dev-only).
2. **External contract** — feature names, tool names, doc headings **without** plan-phase words.

When writing user docs, use the external contract (or a separate outline section), not the phase headings.

## Plan mode / new plans

- **Always** start from [`.cursor/plans/_template.md`](../plans/_template.md); save the new file under `.cursor/plans/` (e.g. `{topic}-plan.md`).
- After acceptance/complete, archive under `docs/dev/` if it should stay in-repo; optionally one line in `.cursor/plans/README.md`.
- Do not place plans next to release docs “for convenience.”
- Optional translations of archives live only under `docs/dev/i18n/` — never under `Documentation~/i18n/`.

## i18n / “translate documents” requests

- Scope of `Documentation~/` = **user-facing** docs only.
- Do **not** treat missing `docs/dev` translations (or absence of a plan under `documents/`) as a gap to fill in release docs.
